.TH XSDL 1 "November 2026" "xsdl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Xsdl \- X server that renders into an SDL window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Xsdl
.RI [ :display ]
.RI [ option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Xsdl
is a kdrive X server that draws into an SDL2 window instead of a display
device. Keyboard and mouse input come from that window. It is useful for
showing X clients from old systems or emulated machines on a desktop that
has no X server of its own.
.PP
The window can be resized; the X screen keeps its size and is scaled to fit.
The screen depth may be 1, 8 (PseudoColor), 15, 16 or 24.
.SH OPTIONS
In addition to the standard X server options (see
.BR Xserver (1)):
.TP
.BI \-screen " WIDTHxHEIGHT[xDEPTH]"
Screen size and depth. The default is 1024x768x24.
.TP
.BI \-zoom " n"
Make the window initially
.I n
times the screen size.
.TP
.B \-fullscreen
Run in a fullscreen window.
.TP
.BI \-title " title"
Set the window title. The default is "Xsdl :\fIdisplay\fP".
.TP
.B \-host\-cursor
Show the host cursor over the window as well as the X cursor.
.TP
.B \-listen tcp
Accept TCP connections, e.g. from other machines.
.SH KEYBOARD
SDL scancodes are translated to evdev keycodes, so the default XKB rules
are evdev with a pc105 model and the us layout; use
.B \-xkb-layout
and related options to change them. On macOS, Option is Alt and Command is
Super.
.SH NOTES
Closing the window terminates the server.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR Xserver (1),
.BR Xephyr (1)
